 =?UTF-8?q?based=20pruning?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Behaviours:
Durable usage history:
- Remove the 92-day scan-cache retention cutoff and prune helper, retain already scanned records even when original transcripts disappear, and keep their directories discoverable for aggregation.
- Preserve existing source aggregation and deduplication, reuse cached record arrays when no tail is present, and cooperatively yield every 1000 cache entries/records during large scans.

Pass an epoch-zero retention cutoff through the current provider reader contract, including the relocated Cursor account cache; verify all-time Cursor fetch, refresh and restart.

All-time web/desktop range:
- Add a persisted all-time range using a 1970-01-01 query start, support it in both period controls and refresh behavior, and trim chart enumeration to the earliest returned usage day or today for empty results.
- Retain hourly handling for the 24-hour range and existing finite-range shortcuts; let all-time appear without inventing a keybinding and update shortcut type handling and Settings keybinding iteration.
- Document all-time usage and indefinite cached history, update retained-source/preference tests, preserve current scan-cache tests and add focused all-time window/chart coverage.

Integration details:
- Preserve upstream v11 scan-cache migration, service-tier reconciliation, route-modal layout, and relocated wide/compact period controls while removing only history-age retention.

- Skip retained deleted-transcript cache entries whose mtime precedes the requested window start, while retaining their records indefinitely for all-time queries. Finite-range source file/session counts exclude those entries; align existing out-of-window source assertions.

- Also preserve interrupted/compressed Codex reconciliation, model-filtered scans and summaries, Cursor API-key authentication and consolidated warning messages.
- Upstream removed the Cursor CLI credential and Keychain fallbacks (#32448), so the all-time Cursor history test signs in through CURSOR_API_KEY like the upstream Cursor tests.

Port to 965ddc1d6c:
- Applied without conflicts. UsageService.ts and usageScanCache.ts did not change upstream; 965ddc1d6c still prunes at CACHE_RETENTION_DAYS = 92 (UsageService.ts:73) and has no all-time range.

Port to 691b9709b0:
- Upstream c03f84bcde streams the scan cache to disk and removes superseded cache files after a save, and 729f6757d9 bumps the cache to v12 and merges repeated Claude keys in dedupeWithinFile. Kept both; removed only CACHE_RETENTION_DAYS, pruneScanCache and the retention cutoffs again, next to upstream's STALE_TEMP_DIRECTORY_MS (temp directories, not usage records). The streamed writer and decodeScanCache drop no entry by age.
- An unreadable or oversized usage scan cache is never overwritten: a current file whose content cannot load (empty, invalid JSON, too long to read) is moved aside to usage-scan-cache-v12.unreadable-<time>-<nonce>.json with one warning and saving starts over; a read failure that says nothing about the content (permissions, I/O) of the current file, or a failed move, leaves it in place and stops saving until restart; older-version cache files are kept after a save, as a fallback that may hold usage the saved cache lacks, and one that cannot be loaded is skipped with a warning while saving continues; the writer refuses a document longer than the loader's string limit, keeping the previous file.

Port to e07585e5fb:
- Upstream #33993 added saved scan coverage (coveredSince) and a provisional from-memory read, #35497 replaces archived Codex cache entries, and #35423, #35497 and #29366 bump the cache to v15. Kept all three; removed CACHE_RETENTION_DAYS, pruneScanCache and its coverage clamp, and the retention cutoff in resolveTranscriptDirs, collectDirs and readSummary again. Coverage is never lowered because nothing is pruned.
- The 1,000-item cooperative yield now wraps upstream's per-folder withinDir check and runs before upstream's saved-file reordering; the unreadable-cache set-aside and freeze keep their place in ensureScanCacheLoaded next to upstream's `current` flag.
- UsageService.test.ts: upstream moved these cases from it.live with TestClock.layer() to it.effect (#35868, #35993). The all-time Cursor, cache-upgrade (now v4 to v14, expecting usage-scan-cache-v15.json), saved-usage and saved-window cases follow that form; the upgrade case still expects the older cache files to stay.

Port to ee4ef06469:
- UsageService.test.ts: upstream #36367 bumps the scan cache to v16. The cache-upgrade case keeps this commit's resave and kept-older-files assertions and now expects usage-scan-cache-v16.json.

